WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.000
Today we'll see how to create this spinning loading animation,

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.180
using Pure CSS.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.700
And, uh, animations like this comes in handy many times,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.900
so we'll quickly see how to make one.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.900
So saying that, let's get into the code.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.100
So we have our basic instrument skeletal structure already.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.800
So I just create a &lt;div&gt; with a class container

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.900
which is for the solely purpose to bring it to the center of our screen,

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.400
and uh

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.200
within this &lt;div&gt;, I'll create one more &lt;div&gt; with the class loading

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.000
where we are going to actually do the animation of loading.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.740
So  I'll do the CSS in this file only,

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.180
so we're doing the style text.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:54.780
First I'll set margin and padding to zero for all the content,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:01:00.500
so I'll do asterisk, and within this I'll set margin and padding to zero.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.040
Next, let's start with a container.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.760
So we want to bring it to the center of our screen

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:10.300
So I'll just do top to 50%, left to 50%,

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.920
position to absolute

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.215
and uh transform, translate -50%

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.820
comma -50%.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.920
So we'll get it in the center of our screen.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.460
Now let's start with the loading.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.440
So I'll create a border of 6 pixel,

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.100
solid,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.780
and a light gray color, so I'll give

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.180
#ccc.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.640
And next, I'll give a width of 60 pixels

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.640
and height of 60 pixels.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.820
So now if you'll save this,

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.660
you will get the box on the screen.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.800
As we have a box,

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.560
to convert it to a circle,

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.000
what we have to do is we have to set the border-radius to 50%.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.720
So now we'll get it in the shape of a circle.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.500
Next, I'll just give a border-top-color

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.920
and a border-left-color

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.920
to a hex value, which will give it a green color.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.920
[music]

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:19.580
Now, for the animation, we are going to use this animation property.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.580
So first is the animation name,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.580
so I'll give it a spin.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.500
Next is the animation duration,

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.020
so I'll give off one second.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.940
And we'll give the animation iteration count to infinite

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.300
so that it loops forever.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:41.500
And the animation timing function to ease-in-out.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.280
So after doing this, we need to set keyframes for the animation.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.780
So we'll use this @keyframes and pass the animation name, which is spin.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.480
So for the 0%,

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:01.380
we will do this transform, rotate: 0 degrees.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:10.020
And for the 100%, we will change the transform to rotate to 360 degrees.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.560
[music]

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:18.320
So after you save this, you will start seeing the animation.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.500
Now, this is just a basic one,

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.835
but you can play around with these things and change some properties

00:03:24.835 --> 00:03:27.700
depending on how you want to show the animation for the loading.

00:03:27.755 --> 00:03:31.000
You can change the animation duration time,

00:03:31.005 --> 00:03:34.215
depending on how fast you want to show the animation.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.060
Now, if you want the same like I showed you in the preview

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:41.680
where there were a couple of rotations between the starting and the ending point.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.020
the changes that you have to make is in the 100% keyframe.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.520
So if you change the rotate to 720 degrees

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.020
then it is going to rotate twice before it comes to an end.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.780
So it will look something like this.

00:03:54.625 --> 00:03:57.755
Now, if you want to make the rotation three times,

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.120
then you have to just multiply it by 3.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.540
So 360 multiplied by 3, it's 1080.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.480
So now it is going to take three rotations before it stops

00:04:06.485 --> 00:04:07.965
and then start again.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:12.165
So if you are doing something like this, just keep one thing in mind:

00:04:12.165 --> 00:04:15.505
you have to be in a multiple of 360 degrees

00:04:15.505 --> 00:04:20.080
because--let's say if I put any random value like 800...

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:27.160
then you can see that it kind of lags before it starts again for the rotation,

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.700
so it doesn't look good.

00:04:28.705 --> 00:04:31.445
So if you want to go it smoothly,

00:04:31.445 --> 00:04:34.285
then you just want to keep it in the multiples of 3.

00:04:34.285 --> 00:04:37.040
And you can change the animation duration

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.360
depending on how fast you want to do it.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.580
So this basically ends the tutorial.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:47.900
And it's quite easy and quite helpful also if you want some loading animation before showing some content.

